# Derivation, OPEN WORLD (spec §7): the docs that block a release tag — specs/
# plans declaring 'Doc impact: contradiction' dated after the previous release
# (?since bound by the runner), for which NO drain has been recorded.
#
# Draining = the release that fixes the affected published page(s), recorded as
# a docgov:ContradictionDrain in tests/docgov-drains.ttl and confirmed by the
# human via RELEASE.md step 2. Evidence-positive and monotonic: a document stops
# blocking only when a drain record is PRESENT. Absence of a drain blocks, which
# is the conservative direction — see 2026-09-08-the-drain-is-a-release-act-design.md
# §3.1 for why the alternative (letting the tag being built move ?since forward)
# was measured to make this gate vacuous rather than merely coarse.
PREFIX dg: <https://w3id.org/iladub/docgov#>
CONSTRUCT { ?doc dg:blocksRelease true }
WHERE {
    ?doc dg:docImpact "contradiction" ;
         dg:docDate   ?d .
    FILTER (?d > ?since)
    FILTER NOT EXISTS { [] a dg:ContradictionDrain ; dg:drains ?doc . }
}
